    - res-A/@source = "/abs/docs/readme.md"                -> STC-ARCH-110a (absolute path)
    - res-B/@source = "docs\readme.md"                      -> STC-ARCH-110b (backslash)
    - res-C/@source = "https://example.com/doc.md"          -> STC-ARCH-110c (scheme)
    - res-D/@source = "docs/../../../etc/passwd"            -> STC-ARCH-110d (traversal)
    - res-E/@master = "C:\PLM\vault\obj123"                 -> STC-ARCH-110e (backslash)
    - res-F/@master = "C:/PLM/vault/obj123"                 -> STC-ARCH-110f (drive-letter-absolute)
    - res-G/@master = "file:///C:/local/obj123"              -> STC-ARCH-110g (file: scheme)
    - res-H/Summary/@source = "/abs/summary.md"              -> STC-ARCH-111a (absolute path)

  None of the Resource elements below carry an administrative.size-bytes Classification entry, so
  the pre-existing STC-ARCH-102a (lotar-stc-archival.sch's Pattern 3) also fires on every one of
  them — expected and unrelated to the URI checks above; not worth padding out this fixture with
  Classification boilerplate just to suppress an orthogonal, already-covered rule.
-->
